# aero - Minimalism, evolved.
============================
aero is a window manager built atop of dwm.
dwm is an extremely fast, small, and dynamic window manager(dwm) for X.

---
** aero is currently a working dwm fork, but will soon turn into its own independent wm**


Requirements
------------
In order to build aero you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (aero is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install aero (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running aero
-----------
Add the following line to your .xinitrc to start aero using startx:

    exec aero

In order to connect aero to a specific display, make sure that
the DISPLAY environment variable is set correctly, e.g.:

    DISPLAY=foo.bar:1 exec aero

(This will start aero on display :1 of the host foo.bar.)

In order to display status info in the bar, you can do something
like this in your .xinitrc:

    while xsetroot -name "`date` `uptime | sed 's/.*,//'`"
    do
    	sleep 1
    done &
    exec aero


Configuration
-------------
The configuration of aero is done by creating a custom config.h
and (re)compiling the source code.
